   ("The Mech story item runs in an isolated browser host that dreyeck provides. The :mech method has no counterpart in upstream (an added method, not a replacement), so it can be defined from any system once the data it reads is reachable."
    "It reads the retained sitemap (SITEMAP-SNAPSHOT) and the retained page JSON (COPY-PAGE-JSON); those are the two seams above.")
   :PLAN
   "1) Seams for retained sitemap and page JSON upstream (or as reusable extension hooks). 2) Create dreyeck/fedwiki-mech with these four definitions under the library package. 3) Add cl-base64 to that system instead of hyperbook/fedwiki (flexi-streams stays: upstream's utilities.lisp uses it). 4) Delete from story-items.lisp. Test: dreyeck/fedwiki-mech/tests (already dreyeck's, in this PR)."
   :DOCUMENTED-IN "docs/fedwiki-mech-story.md" :ORIGIN-COMMIT "99521dc6a8df21fd56fc0e9da25302bfb7b87f3f" :ORIGIN-SUBJECT
